@startuml f4-event-router-dispatch
title F4 — Event Router dispatches via executor pool (ER waits for available slot)

|EX (executor X)|
start
:On startup, REST POST /executors with routing_target, capacity, metadata;

|ER|
:Register executor X
 with routing_target, capacity N,
 in executor pool;
:Initialize slots_in_use = 0;
:Mark executor X as registered;

|EX (executor X)|
:REST POST /executors/:id/ready
 signal available for work;

|ER|
:Receive ready signal;
note right
  ER now treats this EX as having
  N free slots. ER can match up to N
  pending tasks to it.
end note

|ER|
:Match pending task to available executor
 with slots_in_use less than capacity;
:UPDATE task
 SET status=dispatched,
     executor_id=X;
:slots_in_use = slots_in_use plus 1;
:REST POST /dispatch
 to Executor X
 with task_spec and scope_token;

|EX (executor X)|
:Receive REST POST /dispatch;
note right
  EX can receive up to N dispatches
  in parallel. capacity is the number
  of concurrent containers: each task
  runs in its own container, and up to
  capacity containers can be live on
  the same executor at once.
end note
:Pull pre-built agent image (OCI) if not cached;
:Prepare a new container runtime for the task;

|AG|
:Container about to start;
:Read secrets via open env (see F5);
:Start agent loop (see F6);

note right
  EX now runs the task in one of its
  N slots. If slots_in_use reaches
  capacity, ER stops matching to this EX
  until a task completes and frees a slot.
  On completion (see F8) the EX reports
  the result and signals ready again.
end note

stop

@enduml